Changes
=======

v4.0.8 20 August 2026
  * Add an example for parsing a JWK Set that contains a key the build does
    not understand, covering `jwk.IsUnsupportedKey` and
    `jwk.WithStrictKeySetParsing`.
  * Bump `github.com/lestrrat-go/jwx/v4` to v4.4.0, which implements ML-DSA
    natively on Go 1.27, and bump companion dependencies to their latest
    releases.

v4.0.7 24 July 2026
  * Bump `github.com/lestrrat-go/jwx/v4` to v4.2.0.
  * Bump companion dependencies to their latest patch releases.

v4.0.6 1 July 2026
  * Bump `github.com/lestrrat-go/jwx/v4` to v4.1.0.

v4.0.5 7 May 2026
  * Bump every `github.com/jwx-go/*` companion dependency to the
    latest release: asmbase64 v4.0.1; compsig v4.0.2; ed448 v4.0.2;
    es256k v4.0.2; jwkfetch v4.0.2; jwxfilter v4.0.2; mldsa v4.0.2;
    mlkem v4.0.2; reddy-pqchpke v4.0.1; x448 v4.0.2.

v4.0.4 7 May 2026
  * Fix `jwe_filter_basic_example_test.go` (and the parallel
    `_advanced` variant): `jwa.A256GCM` was passed to `Headers.Set`
    as a function value rather than its return value, silently
    dropping the `enc` header.
  * Default JWE examples to `RSA-OAEP-256`. Plain `RSA-OAEP` is
    OAEP with SHA-1 per RFC 7518 and is retained for legacy
    interop only; new code should use `RSA-OAEP-256`.

v4.0.3 28 Apr 2026
  * Switch JWE examples from RSA1_5 to RSA-OAEP+A256GCM (RSA1_5 is deprecated).
  * Various comment / usage clarifications across the example set; make
    jwk_example runnable offline.

v4.0.2 19 Apr 2026
  * Bump jwx/v4 and all companion deps to v4.0.0 stable releases.

v4.0.1 13 Apr 2026
  * Bump companion deps to latest alpha releases (asmbase64 v4.0.0-alpha3,
    es256k v4.0.0-alpha2, jwkcache v4.0.0-alpha2, mldsa v4.0.0-alpha2,
    x448 v4.0.0-alpha3).
  * Add ML-KEM JWE example (mlkem_encrypt_decrypt_example_test.go).
  * Add composite signature JWS example (compsig_sign_verify_example_test.go,
    ML-DSA-65 + ECDSA P-256).
  * Add hybrid PQ HPKE JWE example (pqchpke_encrypt_decrypt_example_test.go,
    HPKE-10-KE / X-Wing).

v4.0.0 8 Apr 2026
  * Initial release. Runnable example coverage for jwt, jws, jwe, jwk,
    and the cross-package jwx readme example, plus ed448 JWS examples.
